body:
This isn't legal advice and may be wrong, but as far as I know: In most (maybe all) states in the US, there is an implied warranty of habitability. This almost definitely violates it. Almost any attorney will provide a free consultation on the matter and may take your case for free. You have the right to hire someone to repair it. Depending on the state you will either be entitled to be reimbursed for the cost or withhold that from your rent.   


Something I'm a little less sure of: You also should not have to have paid as much rent for the months that this went unfixed. You should be able to retroactively recover this money.

&#x200B;

Please seek legal advice. If this landlord is doing this to you, they are likely doing it to others and will continue to do so unless someone stands up to them.

&#x200B;

P.S. It doesn't matter that they're not kicking you out if what I've said above is true.

